WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:03.300
We have a lot of choices
to make about our diet.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:06.180
Add to that, doing
the right thing

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.380
when it comes
to preventing

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:08.700
and treating a
chronic disease,

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.040
fighting a virus,
or losing weight,

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.440
and suddenly our
nutrition choices

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.840
can seem almost
overwhelming.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.240
Well, I’m here to help.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.460
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.981
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:23.221 --> 00:00:24.960
Does it ever seem to you

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.380
that some of us are kept from
living longer, healthier lives

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.281
because of our skin color?

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.060
In our first story,
we look at health equity

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:35.880
and why black Americans
are sicker and die younger

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:38.461
than their white counterparts
on average.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:43.740
During the COVID-19 pandemic,
the death rate for African Americans

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:48.660
was as much as six times
higher than white America.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:53.460
The higher Black pandemic deaths
placed a harsh spotlight on their

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:57.540
longstanding higher mortality and
diminished longevity in general.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:02.280
Unfortunately, diminished
African American life expectancy

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:06.300
predates the COVID-19
pandemic by decades.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:10.860
The Black-white death gap
for women is about 3 years,

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:13.680
and for men closer to 5 years.

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:18.360
The COVID-19 death disparities
may have to do with limited access

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:20.700
to healthy food in predominantly
Black communities,

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:24.360
the housing density,
the need to work or else,

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:27.120
the inability to practice
social distancing,

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:31.380
but also the underlying
burden of ill health.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:35.880
Increased COVID-19 mortality and
complications occur more often

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:40.260
in individuals with pre-existing
conditions like hypertension,

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:44.040
obesity, diabetes, and
cardiovascular disease,

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:48.720
comorbidities that are more
prevalent in African Americans.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:52.200
More high blood pressure,
more diabetes, more strokes,

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:57.600
and more likely to die at early
ages from all causes put together.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:02.640
The question is why?
Why do Black Americans

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:07.020
live sicker and die younger
than their white counterparts?

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:10.860
Well, one big factor is
socioeconomic status.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:14.520
In the United States, race
is closely tied to class,

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:18.300
with African Americans about twice
as likely to be living in poverty.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:22.560
On average, education levels are
lower as well; however, even

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:26.160
among African Americans whose
socioeconomic status is comparable

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:29.580
to that of whites, despite the
higher education and more

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:34.560
socioeconomic resources,
health outcomes are still poorer.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:38.520
Part of that has to do
with lifestyle behaviors.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:42.000
For example, fewer than
5% of African American adults

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.040
met physical activity guidelines.

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:46.800
Smoking rates are
actually comparable,

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:49.440
though African Americans
tend to be exposed

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:53.040
to more second-hand smoke
and have lower quit rates.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:57.300
This may be because they're more
likely to use menthol cigarettes,

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:00.540
which enhance the addictive
potential of nicotine.

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:07.140
Why menthol? Because tobacco
companies target the marketing

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:10.140
of mentholated products
to African Americans.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:15.300
Black lives... Black lung.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:20.820
Similarly, if you look at food messages
on African American television shows,

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:25.020
not only does Black prime time contain
a greater number of food commercials,

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:29.760
African American audiences may
be receiving nearly 3 times as many

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:34.980
advertisements for low-nutrient
junk such as candy and soda.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:38.880
That may be one reason why
African Americans tend to consume

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:44.160
fewer fresh fruits and vegetables and
are more likely to eat junkier foods.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:48.180
Of course, where are you going to get
those fresh fruits and vegetables?

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:52.020
There are fewer supermarkets
located in Black neighborhoods

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:57.120
compared with white neighborhoods,
as in four times fewer supermarkets.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:04.080
What Black neighborhoods do
excel in though is fast food.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:08.340
Predominantly Black neighborhoods
have 60% more fast food restaurants

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:11.880
per square mile compared to
predominantly white neighborhoods.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:16.560
Now, of course, dietary behaviors
alone do not fully explain

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:19.920
the significant differences
in diet-related disease patterns

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:20.940
between racial groups.

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:24.360
There are differences in employment
and poverty and home ownership

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:27.480
and healthcare access, all of
which can affect outcomes.

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:32.160
But while there are certainly many
social and economic factors such as

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:35.940
racism and income inequality that
contribute to health disparities,

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:40.740
there is good evidence that simply
eating a more plant-based diet

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:45.600
could help eliminate disparities in
cardiovascular disease and diabetes.

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:48.660
Here's the diabetes data.

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:52.680
Even after controlling for education,
income, physical activity,

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:56.640
and even BMI, non-Blacks
eating strictly plant-based diets

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:59.280
had 57% lower odds of diabetes,

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:05.520
and among Black vegans, it was
even more striking, 70% lower odds.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:08.460
And that was after
taking BMI into account.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:13.380
So even at the same weight,
Black vegans had 70% lower odds

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:15.360
of diabetes than Black omnivores.

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:20.580
And the racial disparity is
only about half that, 36%.

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:24.120
So the increased risk of diabetes
among Black participants

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:29.160
was on the order of one-third,
while the protection afforded

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:31.500
by vegan diets in this
subgroup was about 70%.

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:37.560
Even just a vegetarian diet that
includes still eating dairy and eggs

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:43.140
may more than counteract the
racial disparity in diabetes risk.

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:47.820
And they're not the same weight.
African Americans have higher

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:51.540
obesity rates, cutting their
life spans by six years.

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:56.100
But Black vegetarians and
vegans have less than half

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:59.880
the risk of obesity, compared
to those who eat meat,

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:03.420
and this is after adjusting for
differences in physical activity.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:07.380
So even at the same exercise levels,
those eating more plant based

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:10.320
had but a fraction
of the obesity risk.

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:12.480
High blood pressure.

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:17.700
In African Americans, hypertension
is the most significant contributor

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:21.120
to their increased cardiovascular
disease burden and mortality.

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:27.240
But Black vegetarians and vegans
combined had 44% lower odds

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:30.780
of hypertension, an important
finding for Black individuals

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:35.160
where hypertension is so prevalent,
with no benefit found for those

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:38.820
who cut out all other meat,
but continued to eat fish.

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:43.740
And the same thing found for total
cholesterol and LDL cholesterol:

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:47.520
cutting odds in half among
Black vegetarians and vegans.

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:51.000
As with non-Blacks,
the researchers conclude,

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:54.420
"these results suggest that
there are sizeable advantages

00:06:54.420 --> 00:06:57.540
to a vegetarian diet
in Black individuals."

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:02.460
What about vegetarians
versus vegans?

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:07.440
The title gives it all away:
"Cardiovascular Disease

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:11.580
Risk Factors are Even Lower
in African American Vegans..."

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:14.580
This is something we've
known about when

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:17.760
Caucasian vegans have been
compared to vegetarians.

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:22.020
However, it was not known
whether African American vegans

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:28.260
exhibited a more favorable
cholesterol profile until now.

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:30.780
Significantly lower LDL
cholesterol in vegans.

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:34.320
Now, of course, the vegans
were also significantly slimmer:

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:38.040
on average normal weight as opposed
to the over-weight vegetarians.

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:40.260
But even after taking
that into account,

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:44.700
those eating more plant based
had significantly lower cholesterol.

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:49.380
So there's tremendous
potential for plant-based diets

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:52.380
to promote health among Blacks
living in the United States.

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:57.120
In fact, they may have
an even greater benefit.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:00.120
For example, African Americans
have an excess burden

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:03.300
of chronic kidney disease, not
only because they have more

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:06.960
high blood pressure and diabetes,
but there are genetic factors:

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:14.040
8% to 12% of African Americans
are carriers of the sickle cell trait,

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:17.820
which places them at significantly
higher risk of kidney disease.

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:21.840
So while Blacks represent a relatively
small fraction of the US population,

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:25.980
they account for more than a
third of all patients on dialysis

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:27.480
due to chronic kidney disease.

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:32.400
And that's where plant-based diets
can come in: shown to protect

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:37.440
against both chronic kidney disease
development as well as progression.

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:42.960
Three-quarters of Blacks
are lactose intolerant, too,

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:49.200
so would again stand to benefit
even more from eating plant based.

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:55.260
It is unacceptable that for decades,
the American healthcare system

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:58.920
has failed African Americans and
other minority communities

00:08:58.920 --> 00:09:02.880
in terms of helping to prevent
some of our leading killers.

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:06.060
But that just makes it all
the more important for them

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:10.121
to take the reins of
their own health destiny.

00:09:10.781 --> 00:09:15.060
In our next story, we look at what role
diet and baby powder may play

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:18.681
in the development of fibroids
and ovarian cancer.

00:09:19.603 --> 00:09:24.120
If you randomly select a group of women
and ultrasound their uterus,

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:28.140
the majority of them have
fibroid tumors by age 50,

00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:32.820
and by most, I mean, more
than 80% of black women,

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:36.180
and about nearly 70% of white women.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:41.160
Half of white women already have fibroids
by their early 40s,

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:42.840
and the same could be said

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:45.480
for African-American
women in their mid 30s.

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:51.000
After getting over the shock
of how widespread fibroids are,

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:55.440
the next question becomes,
why the racial disparity.

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:58.620
Is it diet, stress,
environmental exposures?

00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:01.800
Maybe whatever it is
could offer a clue

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:03.720
as to what causes fibroids.

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:05.880
For example, African-Americans
tend to have

00:10:05.880 --> 00:10:07.800
a lower intake of
fruits and vegetables,

00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:10.920
and fruits and vegetables
appear protective

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:13.580
against fibroids,
particularly citrus,

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:16.680
though not apparently
just citrus juice.

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:20.520
It’s interesting, if you measure
the levels of beta-carotene

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:23.820
in fresh surgical tissue
samples of uterine fibroids

00:10:23.820 --> 00:10:26.940
and adjacent normal
uterus tissue

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:28.620
obtained during hysterectomies,

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:33.480
you find significantly lower
concentrations in the fibroids.

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:36.540
In fact, beta-carotene
was not even detectable

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:38.640
in half the
fibroid specimens.

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:42.000
The same thing is actually
found in cancer.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:46.800
Most cancerous tissues tested
had undetectable levels of beta carotene,

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:49.680
compared to the normal tissue
right next to the tumor.

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:53.520
So, maybe decreased
levels of beta-carotene

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:56.160
somehow plays a role in
causing these conditions?

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:59.520
Sounds like a bit of a stretch,
but you don’t know...

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:02.100
until you put
it to the test.

00:11:02.100 --> 00:11:05.820
But, there had never been a
randomized controlled clinical trial

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:10.260
of fruits and vegetables for fibroids..
until, never.

00:11:10.260 --> 00:11:13.020
They did do a randomized
controlled trial

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:16.980
of kind-of-a-fruit-and-vegetable-
at-the-same-time—tomatoes—

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:21.720
but for the prevention of
fibroids in Japanese quail,

00:11:21.720 --> 00:11:26.760
and most of my patients are
not Japanese, nor quail.

00:11:26.760 --> 00:11:30.720
The action of lycopene,
the red pigment in tomatoes,

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:34.740
“in an animal model may
not accurately represent

00:11:34.740 --> 00:11:37.260
lycopene action in humans.”

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:39.780
And indeed, the Harvard
Nurse’s study found

00:11:39.780 --> 00:11:43.620
no apparent link between lycopene
consumption and fibroids.

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:45.960
So, yeah, fruits and at
least green vegetables

00:11:45.960 --> 00:11:49.320
may have a protective effect,
but we won’t know for sure until

00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:51.240
they’re properly
put to the test.

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:54.120
Vitamin D is another possibility

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:56.580
as to why African-Americans
disproportionately

00:11:56.580 --> 00:11:57.780
suffer from fibroids.

00:11:57.780 --> 00:12:00.180
Women with darker
skin are more likely

00:12:00.180 --> 00:12:02.040
to be Vitamin D deficient;

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:06.420
as many as 80% of black women
may have inadequate levels of Vitamin D,

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:08.760
compared to only
1 in 5 white women.

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:13.260
Vitamin D does inhibit
fibroid cell proliferation—

00:12:13.260 --> 00:12:14.400
in a petri dish.

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:17.820
It may be able to shrink
tumors in your pet rat,

00:12:17.820 --> 00:12:19.260
but what about people?

00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:24.360
A population study did find that women
with sufficient vitamin D levels

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:26.940
in their blood had about a
third lower odds of fibroids,

00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:30.900
consistent with the finding that women
who report lots of sun exposure

00:12:30.900 --> 00:12:32.460
also appear to be protected,

00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:35.280
but until there’s
an interventional trial

00:12:35.280 --> 00:12:37.740
where women are randomized
to vitamin D or placebo,

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:40.500
we won’t know for
sure if vitamin D

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:43.740
plays a role in fibroid prevention
or treatment or not.

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:47.820
African-American women
are also more likely

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:50.940
to sprinkle baby powder
on their genitals,

00:12:50.940 --> 00:12:54.300
which may not only
double the odds of fibroids

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:58.680
but may increase the
risk of ovarian cancer,

00:12:58.680 --> 00:13:01.680
the deadliest gynecological cancer.

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:06.960
Internal memos show
Johnson &amp; Johnson knew

00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:09.600
about the cancer risk,
but still decided

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:11.940
to target African-Americans.

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:15.540
“Think of us”,
Johnson &amp; Johnson said,

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:17.880
“as a lifetime friend
of the family,”

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:23.160
a lifetime cut short, perhaps,
by its baby powder,

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:25.920
or at least so said a jury,

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:29.640
which recently awarded a family
$110 million in damages.

00:13:30.360 --> 00:13:34.140
On top of the $200 million
in verdicts from last year,

00:13:34.140 --> 00:13:36.480
with thousands of
lawsuits pending

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:40.260
after internal memos
revealed that decades ago,

00:13:40.260 --> 00:13:43.500
their own contracted toxicologists

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:46.860
were warning the company that
there are multiple studies

00:13:46.860 --> 00:13:50.520
showing a cancer link,
and anyone who denies this risk

00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:53.220
will be perceived by the
public in the same light

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:56.280
as those who denied a link
between smoking cigarettes and cancer:

00:13:56.280 --> 00:14:03.322
“Denying the obvious, in the face
of all evidence to the contrary.”

